          {
            "id": "tc-problem-section",
            "type": "FeatureSection",
            "props": {
              "title": "The Pattern: One Config Change, Millions Disconnected",
              "subtitle": "Every major telecom outage follows the same script. A centralized update cascades through the entire network. No isolation. No containment.",
              "headerAlignment": "center",
              "columns": 3,
              "iconSize": "lg",
              "iconAlignment": "left",
              "textAlignment": "left",
              "iconColor": "hsl(0 84% 60%)",
              "textColor": "hsl(var(--muted-foreground))",
              "cardBackground": "hsl(var(--card))",
              "sectionBackground": "var(--background)",
              "enableSwipeOnMobile": false,
              "anchor": "the-problem",
              "features": [
                {
                  "id": "tc-prob-1",
                  "icon": "AlertOctagon",
                  "title": "AT&T — 125M Devices Down (Feb 2024)",
                  "description": "A misconfigured network element bypassed peer review. Automated 'protect mode' disconnected every device. 92 million voice calls blocked. 25,000+ 911 calls prevented. Full restoration took 12 hours — not because the fix was slow, but because registration servers couldn't handle 125M devices reconnecting at once."
                },
                {
                  "id": "tc-prob-2",
                  "icon": "CloudLightning",
                  "title": "Rogers Canada — 25% of Canada Offline (Jul 2022)",
                  "description": "A core router maintenance update triggered a BGP cascade failure. 12 million subscribers lost wireless, internet, and TV. The national Interac payment network went down — businesses couldn't process cards. 911 services disrupted in major cities. 19 hours of chaos."
                },
                {
                  "id": "tc-prob-3",
                  "icon": "WifiOff",
                  "title": "Optus Australia — 10M Customers Dark (Nov 2023)",
                  "description": "A routine software upgrade caused a BGP routing overflow. Core routers auto-disconnected in cascade. 10 million customers and 400,000 businesses offline. 2,100+ emergency calls failed. Hospitals, transit, and payment terminals disrupted nationwide. The CEO resigned."
                }
              ]
            },
            "styles": {},
            "children": []
          },
          {
            "id": "tc-stats-section",
            "type": "FeatureSection",
            "props": {
              "title": "The Industry Reality",
              "subtitle": "Telecom infrastructure is more fragile than the public realizes.",
              "headerAlignment": "center",
              "columns": 4,
              "iconSize": "md",
              "iconAlignment": "center",
              "textAlignment": "center",
              "iconColor": "hsl(220 80% 60%)",
              "textColor": "hsl(var(--muted-foreground))",
              "cardBackground": "hsl(var(--card))",
              "sectionBackground": "var(--muted)",
              "enableSwipeOnMobile": true,
              "features": [
                {
                  "id": "tc-stat-1",
                  "icon": "DollarSign",
                  "title": "$9,000/minute",
                  "description": "Average cost of IT downtime in 2025. A 12-hour outage costs over $6.4M before you count reputation damage."
                },
                {
                  "id": "tc-stat-2",
                  "icon": "UserX",
                  "title": "58% Human Error",
                  "description": "Of all human-error outages in 2025, 58% were caused by staff failing to follow established procedures. (Uptime Institute)"
                },
                {
                  "id": "tc-stat-3",
                  "icon": "Phone",
                  "title": "90% of 911 Centers",
                  "description": "Nearly 90% of US emergency communication centers experienced at least one system outage in the past 12 months."
                },
                {
                  "id": "tc-stat-4",
                  "icon": "Zap",
                  "title": "54% Power/Config",
                  "description": "Over half of all impactful outages in 2024 were caused by power failures or network configuration errors — preventable with decentralization."
                }
              ]
            },
            "styles": {},
            "children": []
          },
          {
            "id": "tc-solution-section",
            "type": "FeatureSection",
            "props": {
              "title": "The Edge-Native Antidote",
              "subtitle": "Decentralize risk. Give every tower cluster, regional NOC, and subscriber management system its own autonomous edge.",
              "headerAlignment": "center",
              "columns": 2,
              "iconSize": "lg",
              "iconAlignment": "center",
              "textAlignment": "center",
              "iconColor": "hsl(142 71% 45%)",
              "textColor": "hsl(var(--muted-foreground))",
              "cardBackground": "hsl(var(--card))",
              "sectionBackground": "var(--background)",
              "enableSwipeOnMobile": false,
              "anchor": "the-solution",
              "features": [
                {
                  "id": "tc-sol-1",
                  "icon": "Radio",
                  "title": "Autonomous Tower NOC",
                  "description": "Edge dashboards run independently on SQLite at each cell tower cluster. If central routing breaks, local network monitoring, diagnostics, and technician interfaces stay fully operational."
                },
                {
                  "id": "tc-sol-2",
                  "icon": "RefreshCw",
                  "title": "Graceful Reconnection",
                  "description": "Decoupled architecture prevents the 125M-device-stampede problem. Edge nodes buffer subscriber events and sync incrementally when connectivity restores — not all at once."
                },
                {
                  "id": "tc-sol-3",
                  "icon": "Undo2",
                  "title": "Immutable Deploys & Instant Rollback",
                  "description": "No more failed BGP updates crippling the entire network. Code is pushed as pre-compiled, immutable bundles. If a deployment fails, one-click rollback instantly reverts to the prior known-good version."
                },
                {
                  "id": "tc-sol-4",
                  "icon": "Database",
                  "title": "Crisis Queue Buffering",
                  "description": "During backhaul degradation, bill payments, subscriber activations, and provisioning events don't fail — they buffer. Edge Redis queues absorb the shock and sync data sequentially once connectivity is restored."
                }
              ]
            },
            "styles": {},
            "children": []
